\DOC BIGNUM_RANGE_TAC

\TYPE {BIGNUM_RANGE_TAC : string -> string -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Adds an assumption bounding a named bignum value by {2 EXP (64 * k)}, where {k}
is a named digit count, leaving the conclusion unchanged.

\DESCRIBE
The two arguments are strings: {k}, the name of the variable giving the number
of 64-bit digits, and {m}, the name of the variable denoting the numeric value
held in that bignum. Writing {u} for the variable named by {m} and {k} for the
variable named by the first argument, the new assumption is appended at the end
of the assumption list:
{
           A ?- t
   ======================================  BIGNUM_RANGE_TAC k m
   A, u < 2 EXP (64 * k) ?- t
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces this is the only kind of outcome, and it always occurs
on goals whose conclusion is an {ensures} specification with assumptions
relating the digit-count variables to machine words.

\ENDDOC
